WEBVTT

00:00.007 --> 00:01.675
THIS IS A WORK OF FICTION. UNDERAGE
DRINKING IS STRONGLY PROHIBITED.

00:01.675 --> 00:03.344
FORCEFUL ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION AND
SHAMEFUL ACTS ARE NOT ENCOURAGED.

00:03.344 --> 00:04.970
VIEW THIS AS A COMEDY. ALL CHARACTERS
APPEARING IN THIS WORK ARE OF LEGAL AGE.

00:06.138 --> 00:09.058
Let's help each
other out from now on.

00:10.476 --> 00:11.685
Kouhai.

00:17.274 --> 00:20.903
Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth

00:20.903 --> 00:23.906
Right now is always
the best of the season

00:24.114 --> 00:27.576
Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning

00:27.660 --> 00:31.121
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

00:31.121 --> 00:34.416
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 2

00:34.458 --> 00:36.544
Ever Endless

00:37.753 --> 00:39.421
Ever Endless

00:41.173 --> 00:42.716
Ever Endless

00:44.593 --> 00:45.970
Ever Endless

00:46.637 --> 00:51.433
Mon-Tues-Weds-Thurs-Fri,
my life knows no variety

00:51.433 --> 00:52.852
Ever Endless

00:53.269 --> 00:58.065
Sat-Sun, wake up in the afternoon
with only my smartphone to surf

00:58.065 --> 00:59.650
Ever Endless

00:59.650 --> 01:01.068
All my limbs' been giving in

01:01.068 --> 01:02.903
Kalbi's a burden
like my lumber spine

01:02.903 --> 01:04.488
Doing family
service with irises dim

01:04.488 --> 01:06.115
But you know that
I'll go all the way

01:06.532 --> 01:09.702
Glitter, shimmer,
the light's shining

01:09.994 --> 01:13.539
Let's give it one more chance

01:13.539 --> 01:17.001
Let's ride out into the
highway of our youth

01:17.209 --> 01:20.004
Right now is always
the best of the season

01:20.212 --> 01:23.841
Get high on hope, as
we adults keep winning

01:23.841 --> 01:26.844
Let's take a dive to explore
an entirely new world

01:27.094 --> 01:29.221
Youth is when you never...

01:29.221 --> 01:30.723
stop chasing your own values

01:30.723 --> 01:32.391
Our youth's eternal

01:32.391 --> 01:33.976
the color never fades with age

01:33.976 --> 01:35.853
Youth is when you keep...

01:35.853 --> 01:37.396
getting lost along the way

01:37.396 --> 01:40.941
Youth is Forever

01:45.279 --> 01:48.073
So... do you two
know each other?

01:48.657 --> 01:52.077
Manager, please let
me train the new guy.

01:52.077 --> 01:52.703
Huh?

01:52.703 --> 01:53.704
That's okay, right?

01:54.288 --> 01:56.248
Well, I'm okay with it...

01:56.248 --> 01:58.334
but he doesn't look
like he wants to.

01:58.334 --> 01:59.793
It's fine.

01:59.793 --> 02:02.087
Aren't you happy
I'm training you?

02:02.087 --> 02:03.505
Not in the least...

02:03.547 --> 02:05.257
You're happy, right?

02:05.257 --> 02:07.510
I'm haffy...

02:07.676 --> 02:10.387
Manager, leave the rest to me.

02:10.387 --> 02:11.764
Ah, sure.

02:11.764 --> 02:14.058
Alright, get along you two.

02:14.058 --> 02:15.017
Yes, sir.

02:15.017 --> 02:16.977
You stay here.

02:17.228 --> 02:18.646
Yes, sir...

02:20.564 --> 02:23.609
Call me Sakurako-sama, got it?

02:23.817 --> 02:25.444
Sakurako-sama?

02:25.444 --> 02:27.530
Wouldn't I call you
by your last name?

02:27.530 --> 02:29.907
I hate my last name.

02:30.157 --> 02:31.408
Your last name is...

02:31.408 --> 02:33.160
BUSUJIMA

02:34.078 --> 02:35.246
Oh, it's Busujima.

02:35.704 --> 02:37.456
Who are you calling ugly?

02:37.706 --> 02:39.166
You're so unreasonable...

02:40.834 --> 02:42.545
You don't need
to care about that.

02:42.545 --> 02:44.296
Well, I do.

02:44.505 --> 02:45.798
But still...

02:46.090 --> 02:48.884
no one who looks at you
would think you're ugly.

02:50.719 --> 02:51.846
Hmph...

02:51.846 --> 02:52.596
Any problem?

02:52.930 --> 02:53.681
Not really.

02:54.056 --> 02:55.516
Well, you do have a point.

02:55.808 --> 02:59.186
That's why if anyone tells you
that you're ugly, just say this.

02:59.937 --> 03:02.606
"The ugliness is in my heart."

03:05.234 --> 03:07.194
So what do I call you?

03:07.486 --> 03:10.698
Now that I think about it, having
you call me by my name is also a bit...

03:11.240 --> 03:14.243
Alright, I'm giving you the
right to use my last name.

03:14.535 --> 03:16.704
Understood, then Busujima-san.

03:16.996 --> 03:19.206
Don't you mean Busujima-sama?

03:19.415 --> 03:21.625
So I'm only allowed
if I add "sama?"

03:21.625 --> 03:24.086
If you were hot and my type,

03:24.086 --> 03:26.213
you could call me
whatever you liked, though.

03:26.797 --> 03:30.009
Really... Would you
pardon me for my ugly face.

03:30.217 --> 03:33.095
But you do really care
about appearances, huh?

03:33.220 --> 03:35.264
Huh? Of course.

03:35.264 --> 03:38.350
I'm only interested in good
looks and brand goods.

03:38.809 --> 03:41.228
Now, let's start the training.

03:41.228 --> 03:42.479
Yes, bit...

03:43.147 --> 03:43.939
Busujima-sama.

03:44.273 --> 03:46.525
You were about to say
something, weren't you?

03:46.525 --> 03:48.235
I wouldn't dare to.

03:48.235 --> 03:50.237
CUSTOMER SERVICE

03:50.529 --> 03:53.240
First, I'll have you learn how
to serve customers properly.

03:53.657 --> 03:57.995
Starting now, I will act as a customer
and you will greet me properly.

03:58.120 --> 03:59.496
Understood.

04:00.164 --> 04:01.415
Welcome.

04:03.000 --> 04:04.877
Table for one?

04:08.130 --> 04:09.465
Why are you stripping?

04:09.465 --> 04:12.218
It's rude to serve
customers in wet clothes.

04:13.010 --> 04:14.720
Put your clothes
on and continue.

04:15.054 --> 04:16.096
Understood.

04:16.680 --> 04:18.057
Table for one?

04:18.057 --> 04:19.475
Can't you tell by looking?

04:19.475 --> 04:21.185
Please have a seat over here.

04:21.185 --> 04:21.894
Hmph.

04:22.436 --> 04:23.729
Here's a glass of water.

04:23.729 --> 04:24.396
Hmph.

04:30.277 --> 04:32.321
Why did you light a lighter?

04:32.905 --> 04:35.658
To prove that it
was really water.

04:35.658 --> 04:37.076
You're hopeless.

04:37.076 --> 04:38.827
You don't even know the basics.

04:38.827 --> 04:39.870
The basics?

04:40.079 --> 04:42.998
The basic of customer
service is a refreshing smile.

04:42.998 --> 04:43.916
SMILE!! Uh-huh.

04:43.999 --> 04:46.377
Your smile is disgusting.

04:46.377 --> 04:48.170
Are you looking for a fight?

04:48.379 --> 04:49.964
Welcome.

04:51.006 --> 04:52.299
Now, you try.

04:52.550 --> 04:53.509
Roger.

04:54.260 --> 04:55.678
Welcome.

04:56.720 --> 04:58.180
Sorry, I was wrong.

04:58.180 --> 04:59.056
About what?

04:59.306 --> 05:01.934
I was talking about smiles
and all, but before that,

05:01.934 --> 05:04.019
your face is too
gross to begin with.

05:04.019 --> 05:06.397
I'm fixing to snap
here eventually.

05:06.939 --> 05:08.440
Is it that bad?

05:08.440 --> 05:10.234
Hard to say, but
it's worse than vomit.

05:10.234 --> 05:11.569
What do you mean, "hard to say?"

05:12.194 --> 05:14.196
But how good you look
doesn't even matter!

05:14.196 --> 05:15.447
It so does.

05:15.447 --> 05:18.075
I can't get motivated
working with someone so ugly.

05:18.617 --> 05:21.453
Shut up and listen, you bitch.

05:21.453 --> 05:23.330
Oh? What was that?

05:23.330 --> 05:25.791
If you want to talk
back, then I'm all ears.

05:26.333 --> 05:29.128
You're a loser who got
rejected by the likes of Kouhei.

05:30.796 --> 05:33.257
Busujima-san, how's
Kitahara-kun doing?

05:35.384 --> 05:37.845
Good, stay like that
for 30 more minutes.

05:43.058 --> 05:45.227
That damned sadist!

05:45.227 --> 05:48.647
You were the one that
spilled it, so you clean it up.

05:48.898 --> 05:51.525
Anyone else would
have quit already.

05:51.859 --> 05:52.651
Hm?

05:53.277 --> 05:54.403
Let me help you.

05:54.820 --> 05:55.529
Huh?

05:55.738 --> 05:57.615
Ah, um...

05:58.073 --> 05:59.116
Nice to meet you.

05:59.116 --> 06:01.535
I'm Otoya Naomi, I
work in the kitchen.

06:02.494 --> 06:04.079
Nice to meet you, I'm...

06:04.079 --> 06:06.498
You're the new hire,
Kihara-san, right?

06:06.498 --> 06:08.584
Ah, yeah, that's right.

06:09.084 --> 06:10.628
You don't have to be so formal.

06:10.628 --> 06:13.380
You're older than me, you know.

06:13.547 --> 06:15.090
Huh? Really?

06:15.257 --> 06:16.967
So you're in high school?

06:17.134 --> 06:19.178
Yes. But I'm really glad.

06:19.178 --> 06:19.720
Of what?

06:19.929 --> 06:22.640
That our new hire...
seems like a nice person.

06:24.850 --> 06:27.853
Let's help each other out
from now on, Kitahara-san.

06:30.064 --> 06:31.607
PAST FIRST IMPRESSIONS

06:32.024 --> 06:33.609
THIS FIRST IMPRESSION

06:35.027 --> 06:36.570
Kitahara-san?

06:37.571 --> 06:38.697
So bright...

06:39.365 --> 06:40.658
My eyes are burning...

06:40.866 --> 06:42.660
But we're indoors?!

06:43.077 --> 06:45.287
Hey maggot, are you
done cleaning yet?

06:47.498 --> 06:48.707
What are you staring at?

06:48.958 --> 06:49.875
Ahh...

06:50.125 --> 06:52.211
The face of scum is so relaxing.

06:52.211 --> 06:54.004
I'll chop you up for real!

06:54.380 --> 06:56.257
Good work, Sakurako-san.

06:56.757 --> 06:58.759
Huh? Naomi-kun?

06:58.759 --> 07:01.887
What? Could it be that
you were helping clean up?

07:02.179 --> 07:05.057
Yes, I happened to be on break.

07:05.057 --> 07:06.976
Ehehe, I see.

07:06.976 --> 07:09.144
You're so nice, Naomi-kun.

07:09.436 --> 07:12.147
Don't cause him any
trouble, you piece of shit.

07:12.398 --> 07:15.651
Busujima-sama, you're
not nice at all, you know.

07:15.818 --> 07:17.278
Busujima-sama?

07:17.528 --> 07:19.488
This woman forced
me to call her...

07:19.488 --> 07:22.324
Because Kitahara-kun
insisted on calling me that.

07:22.324 --> 07:26.078
But I still prefer to be
called Busujima-san.

07:26.203 --> 07:28.497
Huh? I thought you
don't like your last name.

07:28.998 --> 07:30.541
Ah, that's right.

07:30.916 --> 07:34.044
Kitahara-kun, you can
call me Sakurako as well.

07:34.044 --> 07:35.337
Huh? Okay...

07:35.546 --> 07:39.216
But you'll call me
Busujima-sama in private.

07:39.216 --> 07:41.427
You're so hard to please.

07:41.677 --> 07:42.887
Ah, that's right.

07:42.887 --> 07:43.596
Huh?

07:43.596 --> 07:45.890
You two are on
break soon, right?

07:46.098 --> 07:48.976
I'll go make some
food for you two.

07:49.101 --> 07:50.519
Huh? But...

07:50.519 --> 07:52.438
Aren't you on break?

07:52.438 --> 07:54.190
It's not as if I'm tired.

07:55.608 --> 07:57.526
Please wait a moment.

07:58.694 --> 07:59.945
Such a good kid.

07:59.945 --> 08:01.197
Isn't he?

08:01.363 --> 08:03.240
Plus he's super hot.

08:03.407 --> 08:04.366
True...

08:05.034 --> 08:07.369
Hey, you wouldn't
happen to be...

08:07.369 --> 08:08.245
What is it?

08:08.245 --> 08:10.039
going after Otoya-kun?

08:10.039 --> 08:11.457
Huh? Is that wrong?

08:11.457 --> 08:13.083
Forget wrong...

08:13.584 --> 08:16.086
There's a huge gap between
your levels of decency.

08:16.086 --> 08:17.087
Huh?!

08:17.087 --> 08:19.798
Give up, there's a limit to how
unsuited you can be for him.

08:19.798 --> 08:22.426
But I'm super
serious about that kid.

08:22.426 --> 08:23.385
Is that so?

08:23.385 --> 08:26.263
So, if you dare get in my way...

08:26.430 --> 08:29.850
Bring it on. You gonna
try and bully me harder?

08:29.850 --> 08:31.936
I'll kill you.

08:31.936 --> 08:32.478
Oh...

08:32.686 --> 08:33.896
That being said.

08:34.021 --> 08:34.939
What now?

08:36.190 --> 08:38.317
To keep you from
doing unnecessary stuff,

08:38.317 --> 08:41.487
I'll torment you
to... ex-haus-tion.

08:45.658 --> 08:47.535
Is work rough?

08:47.660 --> 08:50.246
Yeah, well... in many ways...

08:50.746 --> 08:53.374
It's both tiring
and embarrassing.

08:53.374 --> 08:53.958
Huh?

08:53.958 --> 08:55.167
Embarrassing?

08:55.668 --> 08:57.836
Oh, I better get going.

08:59.296 --> 09:01.090
Well, I'm heading out.

09:01.090 --> 09:03.259
Okay, have a safe trip.

09:04.927 --> 09:07.388
There's something off about him.

09:07.388 --> 09:09.640
Is the part-time job that tough?

09:09.640 --> 09:12.476
I heard it's just a
normal family restaurant.

09:12.726 --> 09:13.727
Hey, Azusa.

09:13.727 --> 09:14.436
Huh?

09:14.603 --> 09:17.064
Can you go check on him?

09:17.481 --> 09:19.608
If something
happens to Iori-kun...

09:20.901 --> 09:21.777
Okay.

09:22.570 --> 09:23.821
What about you two?

09:23.821 --> 09:25.114
I'll go too.

09:27.700 --> 09:28.951
Welcome...

09:28.951 --> 09:29.827
Eh?

09:29.910 --> 09:31.495
We're here, Iori.

09:31.495 --> 09:33.747
What do you mean by "eh?"

09:35.541 --> 09:36.333
Huh?

09:36.584 --> 09:38.127
Is it just you guys?

09:38.335 --> 09:39.587
That's right.

09:39.837 --> 09:42.006
Then let me show
you to your table.

09:42.006 --> 09:42.798
Uhm...

09:43.549 --> 09:45.467
Beautiful mademoiselles...

09:47.428 --> 09:48.971
I-Iori...

09:48.971 --> 09:50.681
What's with that greeting?

09:50.890 --> 09:53.517
Don't say it! I'm
embarrassed too.

09:53.517 --> 09:56.687
But I was told that you had to
when serving an all-women group.

09:56.854 --> 09:59.356
Welcome, let me
lead you to your seats.

10:00.316 --> 10:00.941
Huh?

10:03.319 --> 10:04.904
Busujima!

10:04.904 --> 10:06.697
- You actually did it?
- You bitch!

10:06.697 --> 10:07.865
- You idiot.
- I'll kill you!

10:07.948 --> 10:10.659
Iori seems to have
fun wherever he goes.

10:12.036 --> 10:13.037
Kitahara-san.

10:13.037 --> 10:13.829
Huh?

10:13.829 --> 10:15.748
You're getting the hang of it.

10:15.748 --> 10:17.041
Thanks to you.

10:17.041 --> 10:20.336
It would've been faster if
my trainer hadn't been her.

10:20.336 --> 10:23.005
BUSU AHAHAHAHA

10:23.005 --> 10:25.257
Do you live alone?

10:25.341 --> 10:27.635
Nope, I live at my
cousin's house.

10:27.635 --> 10:28.969
I see.

10:29.678 --> 10:32.097
What are you talking about?

10:32.097 --> 10:34.517
About Kitahara-san's home.

10:34.683 --> 10:36.727
Oh, I see.

10:36.977 --> 10:39.355
What? The struggles
of gathering cardboard?

10:39.355 --> 10:41.857
Don't just write off as my
house being made of paper.

10:41.941 --> 10:44.276
I mean, you live in
a park, don't you?

10:44.276 --> 10:47.488
I live in a diving shop by
the sea called "Grand Blue."

10:47.488 --> 10:49.031
Diving?

10:49.156 --> 10:50.407
What's so good about that...

10:50.407 --> 10:53.035
Kitahara-san, so
you go diving too?

10:53.118 --> 10:55.120
Well, technically...

10:55.120 --> 10:57.498
Really?! That's great.

10:57.498 --> 10:59.291
D-Do you dive too?

10:59.542 --> 11:00.125
Yes.

11:00.459 --> 11:03.587
I may not look like it, but I'm
the captain of a diving club.

11:03.587 --> 11:06.257
If you don't mind, please
introduce me to your shop next time.

11:06.257 --> 11:07.967
I'd love to go diving together!

11:08.175 --> 11:09.385
Ah, sure.

11:09.385 --> 11:11.095
When would be a good time?

11:11.095 --> 11:14.306
Let's see, I need
to ask first before...

11:15.140 --> 11:16.725
I'm coming too.

11:17.017 --> 11:18.936
Absolutely not.

11:19.687 --> 11:22.815
Actually, I'm also
interested in diving.

11:22.815 --> 11:23.858
Is that so?

11:23.858 --> 11:26.527
Yes, I was thinking
of giving it a try.

11:26.527 --> 11:27.486
Otoya-kun.

11:28.195 --> 11:29.321
Yes.

11:29.905 --> 11:31.282
Do you really plan on coming?

11:31.282 --> 11:33.117
It's a perfect opportunity.

11:33.117 --> 11:37.204
If I show a high school boy my
swimming figure, it'll be an insta-kill.

11:37.204 --> 11:37.538
SPARKLE

11:39.748 --> 11:41.584
Good morning.

11:44.795 --> 11:46.547
Welcome to Grand Blue.

11:46.547 --> 11:48.507
We heard the story from Iori.

11:48.507 --> 11:50.718
You're the captain
of a diving club?

11:50.926 --> 11:52.595
Ah, yes, that's right.

11:52.928 --> 11:54.471
Kitahara, meeting.

11:54.763 --> 11:55.389
Yes.

11:55.389 --> 11:57.474
Why are there two
of those things?

11:57.474 --> 12:00.060
There's no helping it,
they've been here all along.

12:00.060 --> 12:01.854
What's wrong, you two?

12:01.854 --> 12:03.355
- Nope, nothing.
- Nope, nothing.

12:03.564 --> 12:05.316
I'll go ahead and say this now.

12:05.316 --> 12:05.941
What now?

12:05.941 --> 12:08.444
If Naomi-kun falls for
them, I'll decimate you.

12:08.444 --> 12:09.737
You're so unreasonable.

12:13.157 --> 12:15.618
Make it so I'm alone with him.

12:15.618 --> 12:17.286
Do as I say, got it?

12:17.286 --> 12:18.370
What's wrong, Kouhei?

12:18.370 --> 12:19.747
Aren't you going inside?

12:19.747 --> 12:23.167
For some reason, I find
it hard to go in right now.

12:23.167 --> 12:24.126
- Huh?
- Huh?

12:24.126 --> 12:25.002
GRAND BLUE DREAMING SEASON 2

12:25.586 --> 12:28.339
Once again, these
two are my coworkers.

12:28.547 --> 12:31.509
I'm Naomi Otoya,
nice to meet you.

12:31.675 --> 12:33.260
I'm Sakurako Busujima.

12:33.260 --> 12:34.970
This is my first time diving.

12:34.970 --> 12:37.097
Please treat me gently.

12:40.601 --> 12:41.185
What's wrong?

12:41.185 --> 12:42.686
Why is he here too?

12:42.686 --> 12:44.396
Ah, you mean Kouhei.

12:44.605 --> 12:46.607
It's fine. Who cares
if you got rejected?

12:46.774 --> 12:48.317
Of course it's not fine.

12:48.317 --> 12:52.947
I want to show Naomi-kun that
I'm a kind, lovely and proper lady.

12:53.197 --> 12:56.242
The thing you have going
for you is being female.

12:56.617 --> 12:57.701
What to do?

12:57.701 --> 13:00.329
I could hit him so hard
he loses his memories.

13:00.329 --> 13:03.707
What a kind and
lovely line of thought.

13:03.958 --> 13:05.668
Well, you're probably fine.

13:05.668 --> 13:07.044
Huh? Why?

13:07.044 --> 13:10.714
All he remembers from
that day is the seiyuu concert.

13:11.048 --> 13:12.842
A stranger I've
never met before...

13:12.842 --> 13:14.385
It's alright, it's alright.

13:14.385 --> 13:16.262
That pisses me
off in its own way.

13:16.262 --> 13:18.681
If you insist, I guess I'll
go punch him to death.

13:18.681 --> 13:21.016
You know, I don't
hate this part of you.

13:23.227 --> 13:24.895
What's wrong, Cakey?

13:24.895 --> 13:25.980
It's nothing.

13:25.980 --> 13:29.316
I was just thinking they
seem awfully chummy.

13:29.316 --> 13:31.819
Really? I would've said
those two are closer.

13:31.819 --> 13:34.196
That might be true but...

13:34.196 --> 13:35.656
That's because
Chisa's really easy!

13:35.656 --> 13:38.576
Kotegawa, you've just been written
off as being easier than Kitahara.

13:38.576 --> 13:41.287
Now, let's put on our swimsuits.

13:43.581 --> 13:47.167
Huh? Kitahara-san, you
used to be afraid of water?

13:47.376 --> 13:49.628
Well, you could say that.

13:49.628 --> 13:51.547
Then why did you choose diving?

13:51.755 --> 13:53.549
Why...

13:54.175 --> 13:57.887
The important thing is
whether you're interested or not.

13:58.637 --> 14:01.015
I guess it's because
I'm interested.

14:01.307 --> 14:02.766
Is that so?

14:02.766 --> 14:03.767
What about you?

14:04.727 --> 14:06.228
For me, it's because of that.

14:06.687 --> 14:07.605
GREAT NATURE AND OCEAN ARE
AWAITING BRILLIANT BLUE WORLD

14:07.605 --> 14:08.564
MYSTERY AWAITS YOU Palau?

14:08.564 --> 14:09.398
Yes.

14:09.607 --> 14:13.444
I dived there as a kid, it's amazing,
and I love diving ever since then.

14:13.444 --> 14:14.778
Wow.

14:14.778 --> 14:15.946
Are you interested?

14:16.280 --> 14:17.656
Palau eh...

14:17.990 --> 14:19.700
I'd love to go...

14:20.951 --> 14:23.329
but I need to get
better at diving first.

14:23.829 --> 14:26.207
You'll be going for the
advanced license then.

14:26.624 --> 14:28.417
Kitahara, come here a sec.

14:28.417 --> 14:31.045
Sorry, let's
continue this later.

14:31.670 --> 14:32.546
Hurry up.

14:33.380 --> 14:34.381
What is it?

14:34.381 --> 14:36.467
Give me your honest opinion.

14:37.718 --> 14:38.677
What do you think?

14:40.638 --> 14:41.388
Hmm.

14:42.431 --> 14:43.807
81 points.

14:44.350 --> 14:46.977
Who told you to
put a number to it?

14:47.645 --> 14:48.938
That wasn't what you meant?

14:48.938 --> 14:50.147
That's not it.

14:50.689 --> 14:52.358
I'm not losing to them, right?

14:52.441 --> 14:54.360
Ah, so that's what you meant.

14:54.985 --> 14:55.778
It's a massacre.

14:55.778 --> 14:57.738
How can it be that bad!

14:58.113 --> 15:00.157
Don't you understand
the difference in levels?

15:00.157 --> 15:01.325
How would I know?

15:01.325 --> 15:03.369
Then let me put it this way.

15:03.786 --> 15:05.788
It's like comparing
me to Otoya-kun.

15:05.788 --> 15:06.789
No!

15:06.789 --> 15:08.791
That's like losing
right from the start!

15:08.791 --> 15:10.668
It's like losing a
marathon by 45 km!

15:10.668 --> 15:13.504
That means you weren't
even in the race to begin with.

15:14.088 --> 15:15.589
Ah, Sakurako-san.

15:15.589 --> 15:17.800
That swimsuit
looks great on you.

15:18.467 --> 15:21.136
Excuse me, where's the restroom?

15:22.388 --> 15:24.890
Your face is pissing
me off, Busujima-sama.

15:25.224 --> 15:27.476
Isn't she being kind of cunning?

15:27.476 --> 15:28.727
Cunning? How?

15:28.727 --> 15:30.437
Didn't you see
what just happened?

15:31.480 --> 15:32.940
You know, Iori.

15:32.940 --> 15:34.066
What's wrong?

15:34.066 --> 15:36.735
I changed into my swimsuit,
but it's so embarrassing.

15:36.735 --> 15:39.655
So at least, I wanted
you to see it first.

15:39.947 --> 15:41.490
That's what I meant by cunning.

15:41.657 --> 15:43.826
That's not how I saw it.

15:44.451 --> 15:45.327
Otoya-kun.

15:45.327 --> 15:45.995
Yes.

15:45.995 --> 15:48.080
Sakurako wants your help.

15:48.080 --> 15:49.290
Understood.

15:50.916 --> 15:52.251
Hmm...

15:52.251 --> 15:53.544
What is it, Cakey?

15:53.544 --> 15:55.838
So you're on first name term?

15:55.921 --> 15:57.214
Oh, her?

15:57.506 --> 16:00.718
I call her something else
when we're alone though.

16:04.096 --> 16:05.014
Now then.

16:05.014 --> 16:07.308
As a rule, diving is
done in groups of two.

16:07.308 --> 16:08.726
So we'll have you form pairs.

16:09.476 --> 16:11.729
I don't want to, but I
guess I'll pair up with you.

16:11.729 --> 16:12.897
Why?

16:12.897 --> 16:14.481
Why not pair up with Otoya-kun?

16:14.481 --> 16:15.524
Huh?

16:15.524 --> 16:18.110
I can't show off my
swimsuit in a wetsuit.

16:18.110 --> 16:20.946
If I mess up, I'll cause
trouble for Otoya-kun.

16:20.946 --> 16:23.115
So you don't mind
causing trouble for me.

16:23.657 --> 16:26.744
I thought you'd mess up on
purpose to have him fawn over you.

16:26.744 --> 16:29.997
It takes a lot of skill to
make acting stupid look cute.

16:30.039 --> 16:31.582
I see.

16:31.957 --> 16:33.626
But you're worrying for nothing.

16:33.876 --> 16:34.835
Why?

16:34.835 --> 16:37.338
Amateur divers must
stick with the instructor.

16:37.796 --> 16:40.424
Sakurako-san, I'll be
your buddy for today!

16:43.969 --> 16:45.638
Please take good care of me.

16:45.638 --> 16:47.097
Let's have fun.

16:47.556 --> 16:49.850
Did something happen
to Sakurako-san?

16:49.850 --> 16:52.728
She's worried about being
different from everyone else.

16:53.479 --> 16:54.980
What's there to worry about,

16:54.980 --> 16:57.608
she should just be more direct.

16:59.068 --> 17:01.612
I don't know exactly
what you're talking about...

17:02.238 --> 17:03.239
but Kitahara-san,

17:03.239 --> 17:06.116
you aren't the type to care
about others' differences, huh.

17:24.385 --> 17:25.511
What a surprise.

17:25.678 --> 17:27.471
To think that kid's
still in high school.

17:27.471 --> 17:28.514
What about him?

17:28.514 --> 17:30.057
His diving skills.

17:30.057 --> 17:32.017
Almost at the instructor level.

17:32.268 --> 17:34.270
Are his buoyancy
adjustments that good?

17:34.270 --> 17:36.397
Or that he didn't use
much air from his tank?

17:36.397 --> 17:38.899
Of course he's good at that too.

17:38.899 --> 17:40.401
But the most important thing's

17:40.401 --> 17:43.279
he made sure
everyone was having fun.

17:43.529 --> 17:46.699
If someone falls behind, he'd go
up to them so they wouldn't get lost.

17:46.907 --> 17:49.618
He pays attention to fish
that are specific to the season.

17:49.785 --> 17:53.372
and skillfully guides the
schools of fish our way.

17:53.747 --> 17:55.082
Those are probably skills

17:55.082 --> 17:58.210
he developed while taking
care of the juniors in the club.

17:59.545 --> 18:01.130
Is what they said.

18:01.130 --> 18:02.506
I see.

18:02.506 --> 18:05.926
So smart and
kind, that's amazing.

18:06.135 --> 18:08.971
So that's enough
already, isn't it?

18:08.971 --> 18:11.557
Why are you trying
casually make me give up?

18:12.057 --> 18:14.351
Could it be you actually
have a thing for me?

18:14.351 --> 18:15.352
Not again.

18:15.352 --> 18:17.855
You and your
nausea-inducing jokes.

18:17.855 --> 18:19.940
We're carrying on, you two.

18:24.028 --> 18:26.280
The seniors were right.

18:26.697 --> 18:29.200
He's keeping everyone
else's enjoyment in mind.

18:29.491 --> 18:31.702
And he's enjoying himself
as well because of it.

18:32.244 --> 18:34.246
They might be pretty similar.

18:36.165 --> 18:38.125
There were a lot
of lionfish, huh?

18:38.292 --> 18:40.377
I really love those fish.

18:40.377 --> 18:43.130
Huh? Doesn't your
club dive in this area?

18:43.130 --> 18:44.590
Ah no, we do.

18:44.590 --> 18:46.300
Then shouldn't
you be tired of it?

18:46.300 --> 18:48.010
Not at all.

18:48.010 --> 18:49.094
Even the same sea

18:49.094 --> 18:51.722
feels different depending
on the day and the season.

18:52.097 --> 18:55.893
That's why I never get tired of diving
in the same spot again and again.

18:55.893 --> 18:57.770
You must be pretty popular.

18:57.770 --> 18:58.437
Huh?

18:58.646 --> 18:59.355
Well?

18:59.355 --> 19:00.981
Uhm... well...

19:00.981 --> 19:03.609
I hear that from
time to time but...

19:04.652 --> 19:06.237
You really are just like Chisa.

19:06.487 --> 19:09.198
Huh? I'm like Chisa-san?

19:09.532 --> 19:11.367
She's amazing, isn't she?

19:12.117 --> 19:15.871
You seem to be surrounded
by very unique people.

19:16.497 --> 19:19.250
Like ocean fanatics, die-hard
romantics and otakus?

19:19.667 --> 19:21.877
And also alcoholic
and strippers.

19:21.877 --> 19:25.089
Thanks to them, people
look at me in the same light.

19:26.340 --> 19:27.424
But you know,

19:27.424 --> 19:30.344
when it comes to people who
are honest about what they love,

19:30.511 --> 19:32.221
I can't say I hate them.

19:34.557 --> 19:35.558
Alright,

19:35.766 --> 19:38.018
good work everyone!

19:40.437 --> 19:42.231
Oh, is that sashimi?

19:42.231 --> 19:44.316
The owner gets some
for free sometimes.

19:44.316 --> 19:46.235
Everything revolves
around fish today.

19:46.235 --> 19:47.027
You're right.

19:47.027 --> 19:48.696
Eat up.

19:49.280 --> 19:50.614
So good!

19:50.614 --> 19:52.867
Ah! You're dripping soy sauce.

19:53.701 --> 19:55.244
I'll go change into
my rash guard.

19:55.661 --> 19:57.121
Where's Otoya-kun's rash guard?

19:57.121 --> 19:59.415
I think it's out on
the drying rack.

19:59.707 --> 20:00.875
I'll show you.

20:00.875 --> 20:02.084
Thank you.

20:04.545 --> 20:05.838
Hmm...

20:05.838 --> 20:07.047
What's wrong, Kouhei?

20:07.256 --> 20:09.967
That scene got me thinking...

20:10.217 --> 20:12.428
Have we met before?

20:12.887 --> 20:14.930
N-No, of couse not.

20:14.930 --> 20:17.308
No, I'm pretty sure...

20:17.474 --> 20:19.101
Hey, what to do about this?

20:19.101 --> 20:20.561
Isn't it obvious?

20:20.561 --> 20:23.022
Just hit him so hard he
gets memory loss, right?

20:23.022 --> 20:25.357
I do seriously...

20:25.357 --> 20:26.442
like this part of you.

20:27.318 --> 20:28.736
Now, now...

20:31.822 --> 20:33.699
Why don't we have a drink?

20:33.699 --> 20:34.617
The fuck are you?

20:34.867 --> 20:36.702
I have a question.

20:36.702 --> 20:37.995
Huh? What is it?

20:38.078 --> 20:41.207
You came here with
impure motives, didn't you?

20:41.582 --> 20:43.250
Huh? So what?

20:43.417 --> 20:44.126
Is that wrong?

20:44.126 --> 20:46.337
I'm not saying it's wrong.

20:47.129 --> 20:49.048
This is just what I think,

20:49.798 --> 20:52.968
but doesn't everyone in a
circle have their own goals.

20:54.386 --> 20:58.098
Just playing at being pals
isn't going to cut it for me.

20:59.975 --> 21:01.227
Nothing to say?

21:01.477 --> 21:02.436
It's true...

21:02.436 --> 21:05.397
always drinking and
goofing around naked...

21:05.397 --> 21:07.107
Always goofing around naked?

21:07.358 --> 21:11.028
This girl's caked-on
makeup and lewd remarks...

21:11.946 --> 21:15.658
Don't tell me you're planning
to get your hands on him?

21:15.658 --> 21:16.617
How'd you know?

21:17.201 --> 21:19.537
Can you not meddle in
other people's business?

21:19.537 --> 21:22.289
Huh? shouldn't that be my line?

21:22.289 --> 21:24.166
What's going on over there?

21:24.166 --> 21:25.626
I wonder.

21:25.834 --> 21:27.586
By the way, what
about Chii-chan?

21:27.586 --> 21:29.630
She went with Otoya-kun
to the drying racks.

21:29.630 --> 21:31.257
That's not what I mean.

21:31.549 --> 21:33.259
Is it okay to leave them alone?

21:33.509 --> 21:34.969
What do you mean?

21:35.135 --> 21:37.054
You're too easygoing.

21:37.054 --> 21:39.932
Come on, he's good
looking and well-mannered.

21:39.932 --> 21:42.434
And they are even
into the same stuff.

21:42.977 --> 21:45.187
Aren't you worried
something might happen?

21:45.688 --> 21:48.357
Sorry for making you
come out here with me.

21:48.357 --> 21:50.317
I don't mind, what
did you want to ask?

21:52.027 --> 21:54.655
I was wondering if there's
a lover in the picture.

21:55.155 --> 21:55.906
Huh?

21:56.907 --> 21:59.618
Sorry for asking so suddenly.

22:00.327 --> 22:02.705
But I really want to know.

22:05.249 --> 22:08.085
Honestly, the most amazing
person I've ever met...

22:09.044 --> 22:10.588
is Kitahara-san!

22:21.682 --> 22:23.225
Wanna talk to you,
wanna talk to you

22:23.225 --> 22:25.102
First I gotta know all
about you, isn't that right?

22:25.102 --> 22:27.062
Ending it off at round
one reeks of boredom

22:27.062 --> 22:28.814
Rounds two, three,
and four is the plan

22:28.814 --> 22:30.524
As the night gets deeper,
true thoughts escape

22:30.524 --> 22:32.443
Let us go on and on
and dive down late

22:32.443 --> 22:35.446
Your history, your scenery, for
me will your pages get slippery

22:35.446 --> 22:37.489
Hey, show me even more

22:37.489 --> 22:39.241
This is my track and
you are the featured guest

22:39.241 --> 22:40.826
We'll forget by the
time when the dawn hits

22:40.826 --> 22:42.286
Being incomplete is perfection

22:42.286 --> 22:44.538
Hey, show me even more

22:44.538 --> 22:46.123
My mouth keeps slipping,
my mouth keeps slipping

22:46.123 --> 22:47.750
Complaint whether
we sober upward

22:47.750 --> 22:49.793
For now, let's ride
high on this feeling

22:50.169 --> 22:56.217
Let's live this moment with all we
can without leaving a single regret,

22:56.717 --> 22:58.427
We are gonna do it,
we go past the limit now

22:58.427 --> 23:00.054
Not just the whole night,
party till the sun is out

23:00.054 --> 23:02.223
Let's fly high

23:02.223 --> 23:02.806
(Let's fly high)

23:02.806 --> 23:04.808
So first, you just strip it down

23:04.808 --> 23:07.102
An exposed and
feral kind of bond

23:07.102 --> 23:10.731
It's the way of life's cycle,
let us go way beyond

23:10.731 --> 23:12.358
The very moment that
we met I drop my shy act

23:12.358 --> 23:14.109
I wanna bare it all and
say what I need to say

23:14.109 --> 23:16.111
Do it now...

23:16.904 --> 23:21.200
This is the magic spell that breaks
down each and every single wall

23:21.200 --> 23:24.662
And once you get used to
it, you won't feel a thing at all

23:24.662 --> 23:26.163
Being without clothes
is a mystery I live in

23:26.163 --> 23:27.915
The drinking and chatting
is flowing more freely

23:27.915 --> 23:30.292
Try it now...

23:30.709 --> 23:34.213
And right before you
realize what's going on

23:34.213 --> 23:38.425
Your heart will catch
right up and finally be free

23:44.932 --> 23:49.937
NEXT TIME: THAT'S WHO YOU LIKE?
